            <ArticleTitle>Triterpenoids from the aerial parts of Lantana camara.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/10286020.2017.1408595</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two new pentacyclic triterpenoids lancamarinic acid and lancamarinin have been obtained from the aerial parts of Lantana camara Linn. They were characterized as 22β-acetoxy-3,25-epoxy-3α-hydroxyolean-12-en-28-oic acid and methyl 3,25-epoxy-3α-hydroxy-11-oxo-22β-senecioyloxyolean-12-en-28-oate, respectively, through chemical transformation and exhaustive spectroscopic studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
